IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- capital gains: the net capital gain (s 102-5, simplified), the CGT
-- discount (ss 115-5 to 115-25, 115-100, 115-102), the main residence exemption (ss 118-110, 118-150), the small business
-- maximum net asset value test and basic condition (c) (ss 152-10(1)(c), (1AA), 152-15), and death (ss 128-10, 104-215, 118-60).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0001 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 24 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave lives. This module answers chloe c080 (Byford sold, 2040), daniel d055 (the East Perth apartment
-- sold, 2038), chloe c085 and daniel d071 (Jarrah sold, 30 June 2050: the discount and the small business concessions) and
-- daniel d093 (CGT on death, 2078). SCOPED to those questions.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Computing a capital gain (cost base, Div 110 and 112), the indexation that replaces the discount for individuals
-- from 1 July 2027 (s 110-36(1A), Div 114) and the deemed sale and reacquisition on that day (Subdiv 112-E); the ordering of
-- losses among residential and non-residential gains (s 102-5 Step 1) and quarantined amounts (Steps 3-4); the foreign and
-- temporary resident percentages (ss 115-105 to 115-120) and affordable housing (s 115-125); partial main residence exemptions
-- (s 118-185, 118-190, 118-192), the six-year absence rule (s 118-145) and deceased estates (s 118-195); the active asset test
-- and the other basic conditions of Div 152 and the concessions themselves (Subdivs 152-B to 152-E); what "net value" includes
-- (s 152-20) and who is connected or an affiliate (an input sum); the cost base rules for beneficiaries (s 128-15).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- capital gains`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `115-5 to 115-25 -- what is a discount capital gain`

-- s 115-10: made by "(a) an individual; or (b) a *complying superannuation entity; or (c) a trust; or (d) a *life insurance
-- company" (complying superannuation assets). s 115-15: from a CGT event after 11.45 am on 21 September 1999. s 115-20: cost base
-- "calculated without reference to indexation at any time". s 115-25(1): from a CGT event happening to a CGT asset "*acquired by
-- the entity making the capital gain at least 12 months before the CGT event".
-- A company cannot make a discount capital gain. Dates are YYYYMMDD; 12 months later is taken as the same day a year later
-- (the encoder's reading).
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a complying superannuation entity`
    `a trust`
    `a company`

GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `can make a discount capital gain` IF
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `a company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity, `acquired on` IS A NUMBER, `event on` IS A NUMBER, `cost base indexed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gain is a discount capital gain` IF
        `can make a discount capital gain` `who`
    AND `event on` GREATER THAN 19990921
    AND (NOT `cost base indexed`)
    AND `acquired on` PLUS 10000 AT MOST `event on`

§§ `115-100, 115-102 -- the discount percentage`

-- s 115-100: "(a) 50% if section 115-102 (about new residential dwellings) applies to the gain; or (aa) 50% if: (i) the gain is
-- made by an individual from a *CGT event happening before 1 July 2027; and (ii) neither section 115-105 nor 115-110 (about
-- foreign or temporary residents) applies ...; (ab) 50% if ... made by a trust (other than a ... complying superannuation entity)
-- from a *CGT event happening before 1 July 2027 ...; (b) 33 1/3% if the gain is made ... by a complying superannuation entity
-- ...; ... (f) 0% if none of the above paragraphs applies to the gain."
-- s 115-102(1): an individual, not a foreign or temporary resident, from a CGT event "on or after 1 July 2027 in relation to a
-- *CGT asset covered by subsection (2)" -- "a *new residential dwelling"; (5) the individual may choose for it not to apply.
-- s 115-1 (guide): "For a discount capital gain from a CGT event happening on or after 1 July 2027, a discount of at least 50%
-- continues to be available if the CGT event relates to a new residential dwelling or to the provision of affordable housing."
-- Foreign and temporary residents (ss 115-105 to 115-120) are outside this encoding: the input says the individual is neither.
GIVEN `who` IS AN Entity, `event on` IS A NUMBER, `a new residential dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the discount percentage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `who`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN (IF `event on` LESS THAN 20270701 OR `a new residential dwelling` THEN 50 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `a trust` THEN (IF `event on` LESS THAN 20270701 THEN 50 ELSE 0)
    WHEN `a complying superannuation entity` THEN 100 DIVIDED BY 3
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `102-5 -- net capital gain (one gain, simplified)`

-- s 102-5(1): Step 1 reduce capital gains by capital losses; Step 2 apply earlier net capital losses; Step 5 "Reduce by the
-- *discount percentage each amount of any *discount capital gain remaining"; Step 6 small business concessions (not encoded);
-- Step 7 the sum is the net capital gain. Simplified to a single gain with the losses applied to it.
GIVEN `capital gain` IS A NUMBER, `losses applied` IS A NUMBER, `discount percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net capital gain` MEANS
    (`the greater of` (`capital gain` MINUS `losses applied`) 0) TIMES (100 MINUS `discount percentage`) DIVIDED BY 100

§§ `118-110, 118-150 -- main residence`

-- s 118-110(1): a capital gain or loss from a CGT event to "a *dwelling or your *ownership interest in it is disregarded if:
-- (a) you are an individual; and (b) the dwelling was your main residence throughout your *ownership period; and (c) the
-- interest did not *pass to you as a beneficiary in, and you did not *acquire it as a trustee of, the estate of a deceased
-- person." (3) "However, this section does not apply if, at the time the *CGT event happens, you: (a) are an *excluded foreign
-- resident [a foreign resident for more than 6 years, (4)]; or (b) are a foreign resident who does not satisfy the *life events
-- test." (Note 1: s 118-190 if the dwelling was used to produce assessable income -- not encoded.)
-- s 118-150: if you build a dwelling on land you own, "(2) You can choose to apply this Subdivision as if the *dwelling ... were
-- your main residence from the time you *acquired the *ownership interest"; (3) only if it becomes your main residence "as soon
-- as practicable after the work is finished" and continues so "for at least 3 months"; (4) for the shorter of "4 years ... before
-- the *dwelling becomes your main residence" and the period from acquisition. The Commissioner's longer time is not modelled.
DECLARE DwellingSale HAS
    `seller is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
    `main residence from acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` IS A NUMBER
    `main residence from then until the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
    `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
    `lived in for at least 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `chooses section 118-150` IS A BOOLEAN
    `inherited or held as trustee of an estate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sale` IS A DwellingSale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the building choice covers the gap` IF
        `the sale`'s `chooses section 118-150`
    AND `the sale`'s `built on the land and moved in as soon as practicable`
    AND `the sale`'s `lived in for at least 3 months`
    AND `the sale`'s `months from acquisition before it became the main residence` AT MOST 48

GIVEN `the sale` IS A DwellingSale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the gain is disregarded as a main residence` IF
        `the sale`'s `seller is an individual`
    AND (`the sale`'s `main residence from acquisition` OR (`the sale`'s `main residence from then until the sale` AND `the building choice covers the gap` `the sale`))
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `inherited or held as trustee of an estate`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `excluded foreign resident or failing the life events test`)

§§ `152-10(1)(c), (1AA), 152-15 -- small business: who can get relief`

-- s 152-10(1)(c): "at least one of the following applies: (i) you are a *CGT small business entity for the income year; (ii) you
-- satisfy the maximum net asset value test (see section 152-15); (iii) [a partner in a partnership that is one]; (iv) [the
-- passively-held asset conditions]". (1AA): a CGT small business entity is a small business entity that would still be one "if
-- each reference in section 328-110 to $10 million were a reference to $2 million".
-- s 152-15: "You satisfy the maximum net asset value test if, just before the *CGT event, the sum of the following amounts does
-- not exceed $6,000,000: (a) the *net value of the CGT assets of yours; (b) ... of any entities *connected with you; (c) ... of any
-- *affiliates of yours".
-- This is ONE of the basic conditions; the active asset test (d) and, for shares, s 152-10(2) are not encoded, so meeting
-- condition (c) does not by itself give any concession.
GIVEN `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the maximum net asset value test is satisfied` IF
    `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates` AT MOST 6000000

GIVEN `carries on a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `you are a CGT small business entity` IF
    `carries on a business` AND `aggregated turnover` LESS THAN 2000000

GIVEN `carries on a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `aggregated turnover` IS A NUMBER,
      `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates` IS A NUMBER, `partnership or passive asset route` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `basic condition (c) is met` IF
        `you are a CGT small business entity` `carries on a business` `aggregated turnover`
    OR  `the maximum net asset value test is satisfied` `net value of yours, connected entities and affiliates`
    OR  `partnership or passive asset route`

§§ `128-10, 104-215, 118-60 -- death`

-- s 128-10: "When you die, a *capital gain or *capital loss from a *CGT event that results for a *CGT asset you owned just before
-- dying is disregarded." Note 1 points to s 104-215: CGT event K3 happens if the asset passes to a beneficiary who "(a) is an
-- *exempt entity; or (b) is the trustee of a *complying superannuation entity; or (c) is a foreign resident" ((2): for a foreign
-- resident only if the deceased was a resident and the asset is not *taxable Australian property); (5) disregarded if acquired
-- "before 20 September 1985".
-- s 118-60(1): "A *capital gain or *capital loss made from a testamentary gift of property that would have been deductible under
-- section 30-15 if it had not been a testamentary gift is disregarded."
DECLARE Beneficiary IS ONE OF
    `an Australian resident individual or ordinary trust`
    `an exempt entity`
    `the trustee of a complying superannuation entity`
    `a foreign resident, the asset not taxable Australian property`
    `a foreign resident, the asset taxable Australian property`

GIVEN `beneficiary` IS A Beneficiary
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `CGT event K3 would happen` IF
    CONSIDER `beneficiary`
    WHEN `an exempt entity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the trustee of a complying superannuation entity` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a foreign resident, the asset not taxable Australian property` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `beneficiary` IS A Beneficiary, `acquired on` IS A NUMBER, `would be a deductible gift but for being testamentary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a capital gain arises on the death` IF
        `CGT event K3 would happen` `beneficiary`
    AND `acquired on` AT LEAST 19850920
    AND (NOT `would be a deductible gift but for being testamentary`)
